/* data/master-vocab-data.js */
/* EVERY WORD THE SITE TEACHES, IN ONE FILE. Generated 10 Sep 2026 by
   merging the nine loaded vocabulary stores; nothing hand-written except
   this header. INERT — no script tag loads it and nothing reads
   GH_MASTER_VOCAB yet. It exists so the post-ship migration to one
   vocabulary file (and then to more target languages) starts from a
   complete, deduplicated lexicon instead of nine partial ones.

   MERGED FROM (loaded stores only):
     data/vocab.js                    GH_VOCAB            773 bank words
     data/gallery.js                  GH_GALLERY          330 picture-words
     data/multi-definitions-data.js   GH_DICT             5 headwords / 13 senses
     data/dictionary-data.js          GH_DEFS             18 definitions
     data/song-words.js               GH_SONGWORDS        550 own words + refs for 17 songs
     data/reader-words.js             GH_READERWORDS      527 own words + refs for 80 pieces
     data/wordlab-words.js            GH_WORDLAB          30 course words
     data/plurals.js                  GH_PLURALS          166 plural rows
     data/position.js                 GH_POSITION_NOUNS   49 nouns with Russian case forms

   NOT merged: data/nouns.js and data/pairs.js (not loaded by index.html;
   nouns.js is a semantic-pass companion, pairs.js is minimal PAIRS of
   words, not lexicon rows).

   THE SHAPE, and why it is multilingual-ready:

     id       stable: 'w<n>' for bank words, 'g:<slug>' for the rest.
     de       the TARGET-language headword — site-wide convention, the
              field is called de whatever the target is.
     gloss    { en, ru } — HER-language glosses, keyed by language code.
              Adding a UI language is adding a key here, not a column
              anywhere else.
     n        bank image/identity number (numbered 3x3 sheets).
     sheet/pos named-sheet image address (gallery batches).
     imgN     an image number carried by a song/reader word.
     cats     category ids (gallery categories + the bank's cat).
     rg       Russian gender where the bank recorded it.
     kind     word/phrase/verb where a source said.
     plural   { pl, p } from data/plurals.js.
     ruCase   { g, i, p } Russian case forms (position game).
     datForm  weak-masculine dative (dem Bären).
     def      { de, en, ru } one definition.
     senses   multi-meaning words: [{ sid, de, gloss{}, def{}, img, primary }].
     s        example sentences [{ de, en, ru, gap? }] — gap is Word Lab's
              blanked variant.
     alsoN    further bank numbers when two bank rows shared one German —
              both identities preserved for the migration.
     images   further pictures when one word has more than one drawing
              (the two Leaf entries are genuinely different crops).
     noGame   song-words' exclusion flag, preserved.
     src      which stores contributed — the audit trail for migration.

   refs = which activity uses which words, by German headword:
     refs.songs[audioId]   -> [de, ...]   (from song-words.js)
     refs.pieces[pieceId]  -> [de, ...]   (from reader-words.js)
     refs.wordlabOrder     -> [de, ...]   (course order, wordlab-words.js)

   MIGRATION ORDER (post-ship, one consumer at a time — see
   vocab-inventory.md in the drop for the per-file map):
   packs.js first (it already merges GH_DICT over GH_VOCAB — this file
   does that merge once, ahead of time), then songvocab/readerwords
   resolvers, then the single-purpose readers (mehrzahl, placement,
   dictview), each verified live before the old file is dropped. */

